    "q-159906": {
      "dom_id": "step-q159906",
      "name": "Question 11",
      "problem": "Let $X=[{X}_{1},{X}_{2},{X}_{3}]^{T}$ be a multivariate normal random vector with mean vector $\\mu $ and covariance matrix $Σ$ given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mu =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,Σ=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the distribution of $Y=-{X}_{1}+{X}_{2}-2{X}_{3}.$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that if $X=[{X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{k}]^{T}$ is a multivariate normal random vector with mean vector $\\mu $ and covariance matrix $Σ,$ then the random variable $Y,$ defined as\n\n$$\nY={c}^{T}X={\\sum }_{i=1}^{k}{c}_{i}{X}_{i}\n$$\n\nis a normally distributed random variable, where $c$ is any $k\\times 1$ column vector, and  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}E[Y] & ={c}^{T}\\mu , \\\\ Var[Y] & ={c}^{T}Σc.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, since we wish to know the distribution of $Y=-{X}_{1}+{X}_{2}-2{X}_{3},$ we have \n\n$$\nc=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, for the mean of $Y,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[Y] & ={c}^{T}\\mu  \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =-1+3+2 \\\\  & =4,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand for the variance of $Y,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[Y] & ={c}^{T}Σc \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}5 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =6-1+14 \\\\  & =19.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\nY∼N(4,19).\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
