    "q-159788": {
      "dom_id": "step-q159788",
      "name": "Question 13",
      "problem": "Let $X=[{X}_{1},{X}_{2},{X}_{3}]^{T}$ be a multivariate normal random vector with mean vector $\\mu $ and covariance matrix $Σ$ given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mu =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,Σ=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 5 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 7\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the distribution of $Y={X}_{1}-{X}_{2}+3{X}_{3}.$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that if $X=[{X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{k}]^{T}$ is a multivariate normal random vector with mean vector $\\mu $ and covariance matrix $Σ,$ then the random variable $Y,$ defined as\n\n$$\nY={c}^{T}X={\\sum }_{i=1}^{k}{c}_{i}{X}_{i}\n$$\n\nis a normally distributed random variable, where $c$ is any $k\\times 1$ column vector, and  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}E[Y] & ={c}^{T}\\mu , \\\\ Var[Y] & ={c}^{T}Σc.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, since we wish to know the distribution of $Y={X}_{1}-{X}_{2}+3{X}_{3},$ we have \n\n$$\nc=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, for the mean of $Y,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[Y] & ={c}^{T}\\mu  \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =2-2-3 \\\\  & =-3,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand for the variance of $Y,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[Y] & ={c}^{T}Σc \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 5 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 7\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 20\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =9-5+60 \\\\  & =64.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\nY∼N(-3,64).\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
