    "q-159794": {
      "dom_id": "step-q159794",
      "name": "Question 14",
      "problem": "Let $X=[{X}_{1},{X}_{2},{X}_{3}]^{T}$ be a multivariate normal random vector with mean vector $\\mu $ and covariance matrix $Σ$ given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mu =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,Σ=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 5\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the distribution of $Y=-{X}_{1}+3{X}_{2}+2{X}_{3}.$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that if $X=[{X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{k}]^{T}$ is a multivariate normal random vector with mean vector $\\mu $ and covariance matrix $Σ,$ then the random variable $Y,$ defined as\n\n$$\nY={c}^{T}X={\\sum }_{i=1}^{k}{c}_{i}{X}_{i}\n$$\n\nis a normally distributed random variable, where $c$ is any $k\\times 1$ column vector, and  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}E[Y] & ={c}^{T}\\mu , \\\\ Var[Y] & ={c}^{T}Σc.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, since we wish to know the distribution of $Y=-{X}_{1}+3{X}_{2}+2{X}_{3},$ we have \n\n$$\nc=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, for the mean of $Y,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[Y] & ={c}^{T}\\mu  \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =0+9+4 \\\\  & =13,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand for the variance of $Y,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[Y] & ={c}^{T}Σc \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 14 \\\\ 15\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =-5+42+30 \\\\  & =67.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\nY∼N(13,67).\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
